From cccb249498bd17901d43b0b320f11b578e665bb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:00:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Project DS4.1's vocabulary heads with TileLang in the
 TileLang backend

The packed BF16 head decodes its 12-bit bytes in shared memory and runs a
TileLang GEMM, adding the out-of-window values after the dot product; BF16
heads (the DSpark Markov projection) run TileLang's BF16 GEMM. Each head's
kernels are compiled when it is prepared, one per token tile, and a token's
logits do not depend on the batch. B12X's vocabulary projections now serve
only the B12X backend.
